-- title:
--   Spreading out equality of rigidified-pair points to a basic open
-- statement:
--   The statement is formulated inside the full Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation frame; the many binders are grouped below, and every group is named.
--
--   **Arithmetic base.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$ and a level $N \neq 0$ with $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), with an irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, with $\#(\mathcal O/\pi) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$ (so $\mathcal O$ is absolutely unramified with residue cardinality $r$), together with a fraction field $K_0$ of characteristic zero. A characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-automorphism $Fr$, such that $Onr$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $(\pi)$ is maximal in $Onr$, every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ has a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$; thus $Onr/\pi$ plays the role of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb F_r$ and $Fr$ of the Frobenius. A homomorphism $vdet : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with $vdet(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion side and moduli schemes.** Rationals $a,b$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (division at a finite place $v$ precisely when $v$ lies above $r$ or $\bar r$), a maximal order $\Lambda$ (an order, i.e. containing $1$, multiplicatively closed, $\mathbb Q$-spanning and finitely generated, maximal among orders), an element $\mu_\Lambda \in \Lambda$ with $\mu_\Lambda^2 = -r\bar r$, a map $star_\Lambda$ on $\Lambda$ with $\mu_\Lambda\, star_\Lambda(x) = \bar x\, \mu_\Lambda$, and invertibility of $2$ in $\mathcal O$. A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point rule $pt$ on fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$ (`FakeEllipticCurve Λ N S`), and `h𝒳 : IsCoarseModuli`, whose five clauses assert invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property among such point rules. An auxiliary level $n \ge 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$, $\gcd(n,N) = 1$, a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point rule $ptF$ on curves with full level-$n$ structure and `hM : IsFineModuli` (isomorphism invariance, base change, bijectivity of $ptF$ on all $\mathcal O$-algebras), and a group $G$ acting on $M$ by $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ satisfying `hρ : IsLevelTwistAction` (the automorphisms lie over the base; twisting the level structure by $\chi(g)$ moves $ptF$-points by $\rho(g)$; $\chi$ is multiplicative and unital modulo $n$, surjective onto the classes invertible mod $n$ and injective mod $n$). A forgetful morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, invariant under $\rho$, compatible with $pt$ and $ptF$.
--
--   **Hecke tower and Atkin–Lehner involutions.** For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point rule $ptT$ on curves with extra $\ell$-level and `IsCoarseModuliT`, together with degeneracy maps $d_0(\ell), d_1(\ell) : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base, $d_0$ forgetting the extra level and $d_1$ taking the quotient by any level-$\ell$ isogeny. Endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base which on points send $pt(E)$ to $pt(E')$ whenever $E'$ is an Atkin–Lehner quotient of $E$ at $r$, resp. at $\bar r$.
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite ($a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$) and ramified exactly at $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) with $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$; an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that the meet order $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0 : \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$; a finite place $v$ above $r$. A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ equal to the group of units which at every finite place $w \neq v$ lie in the group generated by the local box units of $R_1$. Elements $s_\ell$ and adelic units $sf_\ell$ for each $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ satisfying `hs` (four clauses: $sf_\ell$ has component $s_\ell$ at every place not above $r$, component $1$ at the places above $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$), with $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$. A unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$.
--
--   **Special fibre and its $\Gamma_t$-action.** The hypothesis that all integers lie in $\Lambda$, and a coordinate map $coord : \Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r^2} \times \mathbb Z_{r^2}$ satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (additive, unital, multiplicative for the Frobenius-twisted product, injective, $r$-adically dense, and trace-compatible). A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ over $Onr/\pi$ of height $4$ (multiplication by $r$ has kernel degree $r^4$), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the identity of $A_0$, with $A_0$ a formal module via $coord$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. Families $e,e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$ with degrees $deg$ and: `hE1` (each pair $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure); `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $\gamma \mapsto e\gamma$ up to $r$-power multiplications); `hE1sc` (rational integer scalars in $\Gamma_t$ act by the corresponding scalars, up to $r$-powers); `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ is a scalar up to an $r$-power then $\gamma$ is a scalar); `hE2` (for every injective ring embedding $E_0$ of the centraliser of the $\mathcal O_D$-action on $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma$ is realised on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0(\varepsilon) = r^{k_\gamma}\, g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$); `hE3` (for each full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ a labelling $\Gamma_t \to \Lambda$ describing the action on $P_0$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$); `hE4` (on any geometrically algebraically closed pullback of $A_0$, every $r$-power isogeny endomorphism preserving the level comes from some $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ up to $r$-powers). An order $R_2 \le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators relative to $R_1$, endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ indexed by $R_2$, and `hE5a`–`hE5e` (additivity, $\Lambda$-equivariance and level preservation of $\hat e$; $\hat e$ unital, multiplicative and integer-compatible; the norm–star relation; agreement of $\hat e$ with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma_t$; and a joint formal realisation of the $\Gamma_t$-action and of $R_2$ with a single $g$).
--
--   **Drinfeld side and the dictionary.** A ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to Onr$; a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ of height $4$; a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ satisfying Zariski descent; a rule $\eta$ sending rigidified data $(X,n,\rho)$ over $r$-nilpotent $Onr$-algebras to $MD$-points, with `hη` (three clauses: on admissible data $\eta$ separates exactly the isomorphism classes, $\eta$ is natural in the base, and every $MD$-point is represented by admissible data after passing to a standard Zariski cover); an injective embedding $E_0$ of the centraliser of the $\mathcal O_D$-action on $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise sense of `hE₀`. A dictionary $eD$ sending points of the functor $G(MD)$ over Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent to pairs (an $Onr$-algebra structure, a Deligne datum for $(K_0,\pi)$), which is natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), compatible with the first projection (`hfstD`), transforms the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` into the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (`hGLD`), turns $\pi$-translation into a Frobenius twist of the first component (`hPiD`), admits $\pi$-translates (`hPiexD`), together with the boundedness hypothesis `hbdd`: for each pair of full lattices $M' \le M$ with $\pi M \subseteq M'$ there is a bound $N_\gamma$ such that over any Artinian local Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra with algebraically closed residue field and $\pi$ nilpotent, every point whose Deligne datum lies in the edge chart $(M',M)$ is represented by admissible rigidified data $t$ with $t.n \le N_\gamma$. A reduction map $\kappa : Onr/\pi \to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps, and an isogeny $\beta_0$ of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$. A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner datum on the special fibre.** A fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $Onr/\pi$ with morphisms $aw,aw'$ exhibiting $A_{0w}$ as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$, morphisms $bw,bw'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ from $A_{0w}$ to $A_0$ with $bw$ preserving the level, and `hJOINTw`: a single $g$ realising simultaneously the $\Gamma_t$-action as in `hE2` and the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$ by an element $\varepsilon_w$ with $E_0(\varepsilon_w) = r^{k}\,g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The comparison map $\Xi$.** A rule $\Xi$ assigning to each rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent a $G$-point of $MD$, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the structure map of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullback), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves, up to $r$-power shifts in the comparison isogeny) and `hΞdef` (an explicit description: an index $j \le 1$ and admissible rigidified data $t$ with $t.X = X$, transported from $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$, with $\Xi$ equal to the triple built from the $(-j)$-th Frobenius twist of $\psi$ and $\eta(t)$). An element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` (over connected $B$, translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds under $\Xi$ to acting by $r^{c} g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$) and `heqW` (over connected $B$ with $\bar r$ invertible, an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ compatible with $aw$ followed by $bw$ corresponds under $\Xi$ to acting by $r^{c} g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$).
--
--   **The rigidified-pair point functor over $C$.** A Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\chi_C : Onr \to C$; a functor $PR$ from $C$-algebras to types; a point rule $ptR$ assigning to each $C$-algebra $S$ whose $Onr$-structure map is induced by $\chi_C$, each full level-$n$ curve $u$ over $S$ and each rigidification $\rho$ of $u$ relative to $(r,\pi,A_0)$ an element of $PR(S)$, subject to: `hR2` (naturality under pullbacks of $(u,\rho)$ along $C$-algebra maps), `hR3s` (every element of $PR(S)$ arises from some $(u,\rho)$), `hR3i` (over connected $S$, two pairs with the same $ptR$-value are isomorphic, the comparison of rigidifications being up to $r$-power shifts), `hR1` (the converse: isomorphic pairs have the same $ptR$-value). A natural transformation $\theta$ from $PR$ to the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}$ (`hθnat`) which on points is the pullback along $(g_0^{-1})^{-1}$ of the second component of $eD \circ \Xi$ (`hθ`). A map $toM$ from $PR$-points to points of the base change of $M$ along $\mathcal O \to C$, natural (`hR0`) and compatible with $ptF$ (`hR4`). Finally: `hsh` ($PR$ is a Zariski sheaf: unique gluing of matching families over standard open covers), `het'` (unique lifting of $PR$-points along a surjection with square-zero kernel, once a lift of the $toM$-image is given), `hred` (unique lifting of $PR$-points along reduction modulo the image of $\pi$, once a lift of the $toM$-image is given), and a system of strata $Xs_d \to M\times_{\mathcal O} C$ with structure morphisms $\xi_d$ locally of finite presentation and formally unramified, point rules $pts$ and $ptX$, subject to `hs0` (the image of $\pi$ vanishes on any algebra carrying a stratum point), `hs1` ($toM \circ pts$ is $\xi_d$ composed with the given point), `hs2` (naturality of $pts$), `hx1` ($pts \circ ptX = ptR$), `hx2` (naturality of $ptX$), `hx3` (every stratum point comes from some $(u,\rho)$ with $\rho.d = d$), `hx4` (equality of $ptX$-values is equivalent to an isomorphism of the level structures together with a strict comparison of rigidifications), and `hs4` (a $PR$-point lies in the image of $pts$ for the index $d$ exactly when the pair admits a rigidification of index $d$ with the same $ptR$-value). An element $g_\pi \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ equal to $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under all of the above: for every commutative Noetherian ring $A$ equipped with a $C$-algebra structure and an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure forming a scalar tower $\mathcal O \to C \to A$, such that the image of $\pi$ in $A$ is zero, for every prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $A$, for every $C$-algebra $L$ which is an $A$-algebra forming a scalar tower $C \to A \to L$ and is a localisation of $A$ at $\mathfrak p$, and for all $x, x' \in PR(A)$ whose images under the map $PR(A) \to PR(L)$ induced by the structure morphism $A \to L$ coincide, there exist an element $f \in A$ with $f \notin \mathfrak p$ and a commutative ring $A_f$, carrying an $A$-algebra structure and a $C$-algebra structure forming a scalar tower $C \to A \to A_f$ and being a localisation of $A$ away from $f$, such that the images of $x$ and $x'$ under $PR(A) \to PR(A_f)$ coincide.
--
--   The localisation $A_f$ is produced existentially, rather than the conclusion being asserted for every ring with the stated localisation property.
--
--   This is the spreading-out (local finite presentation at primes) property of the functor of rigidified pairs $P_R$ attached to the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation frame: equality of two $P_R$-points over the local ring at a prime already holds over a basic open neighbourhood of that prime. It feeds the globalisation step [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_represents_inEdgeChart_of_rigidifiedToG_of_bdd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.exists_represents_inEdgeChart_of_rigidifiedToG_of_bdd), where a $P_R$-point must be exhibited over a base from data given only locally, and rests on the corresponding statement for the strata schemes `exists_strata_point_specMap_comp_eq_of_atPrime_map_eq_of_rigidifiedToG` together with the scheme-theoretic spreading-out lemma [`AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.exists_forall_away_specMap_comp_eq_of_atPrime_specMap_comp_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Spec.exists_forall_away_specMap_comp_eq_of_atPrime_specMap_comp_eq).
